# Line endings for the directories the test suite reads from disk.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. A large part of the suite asserts on source it opens by
# path, and several of those assertions span a newline — e.g.
# `assert.ok(TAB.includes("const panel: React.CSSProperties = {\n  minWidth: 0,"))`.
# Every tracked text blob in this repository is stored with LF, but on Windows
# with `core.autocrlf=true` and no rule here, checkout rewrites the working copy
# to CRLF, those assertions stop matching, and a fresh clone fails three tests
# that pass everywhere the working copy is LF. That is not a content regression —
# the blobs are byte-identical either way — but it makes the suite depend on how
# a machine happened to check the repository out, which a test suite must not.
#
# SCOPE IS THE EVIDENCE, NOT A BLANKET POLICY. This is deliberately not a
# repository-wide `* text=auto eol=lf`. The tests open 57 source files by path,
# and every one of them lives under `src/`, `scripts/` or is `package.json`;
# `tests/` is here because tests/drawer-dismiss.test.ts reads
# tests/responsive-shell.test.ts. Everything outside these paths keeps whatever
# line-ending policy it had.
#
# NO COMMITTED CONTENT CHANGES. Not one of the 211 tracked text blobs contains a
# CR today, so `eol=lf` cannot rewrite any of them; it only stops checkout from
# introducing CRs. `text=auto` leaves genuinely binary files alone.

src/**       text=auto eol=lf
tests/**     text=auto eol=lf
scripts/**   text=auto eol=lf
package.json text=auto eol=lf
